{
  "configuration_id": "config_030",
  "reason": "The only multimodal experiment so far (config_031: scvi_n200, resnet50, avgpool, weighted) achieved 0.678 acc, ~2.5pp above the best RNA-only (config_006: 0.653). This is promising but based on a single data point, and we cannot yet tell whether the gain is robust or an artifact of the weighted fusion choice. Config_030 is identical to config_031 except fusion changes from weighted to concat, making it a clean single-variable comparison that isolates the effect of fusion strategy. If concat yields similar performance, the multimodal gain is confirmed as robust and we can confidently build on it; if it degrades substantially, weighted fusion is identified as a critical design choice. Under a limited budget, this experiment maximally reduces uncertainty about the most promising direction (multimodal + scvi_n200 + multiprofile) before committing further experiments to variations on that path."
}

